<title>GREECE: Delos, International lead Greek balanced funds July.</title>
<headline>Delos, International lead Greek balanced funds July.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delos and International mutual funds were the top performers among Greece's 17 balanced funds at the end of July with returns of 77.46 and 53.65 percent, respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Delos equity-income fund continued to better the bourse's benchmark index in July, the only outperformer.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange's general index started the year at 954.54 and gained 643.8 points or 67.45 percent to 1,598.34 points at the end of July.</p>
<p>Balanced funds under management reached 72.5 billion drachmas in end-June, up 80.02 percent since the beginning of the year and 6.67 percent on June.</p>
<p>They made up 1.71 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.68 trillion drachmas, an increase of 4.93 percent on the previous month and 50.80 percent since the start of the year.</p>
